From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sm64ar <sm64ar@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Library seams and host hooks

Lets a host embed the game as a library and drive it tick by tick.

- pc_main: sm64coop_boot runs everything up to the main loop (returns 0 when
  no valid ROM is found) and sm64coop_tick performs exactly one 30 Hz step:
  network, game, Lua, audio and one render, with no interpolation or sleep.
  With SM64_AR_LIBRARY the desktop main() and the SDL/GL backend selection
  are left out, so the dummy window/render APIs and audio_null stay in use.
- network: a host can run as server without binding a socket (single
  player, no UDP), and in library mode the area timer advances once per
  unpaused tick instead of following the wall clock, so replays are
  deterministic.
- controller: an injection hook supplies the pad state each tick; while it
  is set the physical pads are ignored.
- an accessor for the file-static RNG seed (determinism checks) and an
  override for the resource path.

The desktop build behaves as before.
